    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d979">

                <pb facs="0893" n="885" xml:id="pg885"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/16001: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-29T18:00:00-04:00">June 29, 1940—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>233. Chungking’s 300, June 26, 8 p.m., and 302, June 27, 4 p.m., bombing of
                    Chungking and 303, June 28, 7 p.m.<anchor n="85" xml:id="d979-f1"/> The
                    Department authorizes you, in your discretion and as occasion and appropriate
                    opportunity therefor occur, to continue to bring to the attention of appropriate
                    officers of the Japanese Foreign Office this Government’s attitude as repeatedly
                    expressed, both upon broad humanitarian grounds and upon the ground of danger to
                    American life and property, toward bombings of civilian populations such as
                    those reported in the telegrams under reference.</p>
                <p>Sent to Tokyo via Peiping. Repeated to Chungking and Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
